          "page": 411,
          "section": "Experimental Procedure",
          "quote": "The as-casted Ti –6.2Al–3Sn–5Zr–0.5Mo–1.0Nb–0.4Si–0.2Er titanium alloy was isothermally compressed on a Gleeble-3500 simulator. The cylindrical specimens were 10.0 mm in diameter and 15.0 mm in height. The isothermal compressed temperature was raged from 920 to 1070 °C at 30 °C intervals, and the strain rates was 0.001 –10 s −1. The cylindrical specimens were heated to the corresponding testing temperature with a constant heating rate of 10 °C s −1, and kept for 300 s before the isothermal compression so as to acquire a uniform deformation temperature in the entire specimen.",
